  "moving_average_derivation": "Frame = the current row and the two rows before it in (day, shift) order within the machine. avg3 = sum of the non-NULL units in the frame divided by the count of non-NULL units, rounded half-up to 2 decimals; measured = non-NULL units in the frame; rows_in_frame = all rows in the frame; complete = rows_in_frame = 3. M1 sequence 50,40,55,45,NULL,50,60,30: 50/1; 90/2=45; 145/3=48.33; 140/3=46.67; (55+45)/2=50; (45+50)/2=47.5; (50+60)/2=55; 140/3=46.67. M2 sequence 30,30,35,40,20,45,25: 30; 30; 95/3=31.67; 105/3=35; 95/3=31.67; 105/3=35; 90/3=30.",
